// The rewind to 1950 (0.17.0): the game's opening for a new player. A port of
// the maclaine.se homepage transition (assets/home/transitions/tunnelbana.js)
// that ends on the live game instead of on captures of it.
//
// What it draws, at the played 5.6 s (the homepage timeline at 1.75 times):
// 1. Today's metro spreads out from T-Centralen in the game's line colours on
//    the game's ground, and a year counter comes up at the top left, on 2026.
// 2. Rewind. The counter rolls back like an odometer and the network comes
//    apart in the reverse order it was built: every section goes in the year
//    it opened, the newest first (Skarpnäck, 1994). A section shrinks back
//    towards the older network it joined; a link between two older pieces
//    opens from the middle. What has gone stays as a faint dashed plan, the
//    colour drains and the camera closes in on what is left.
// 3. 1950. Only Slussen to Hökarängen is left, the line that opened on
//    1 October 1950. It comes back in the game's green with a glow, the first
//    train runs down it, its ends are named and the date is set.
// 4. The game. The camera settles on the game's own opening camera while the
//    real map is driven to the same camera frame by frame, so the drawing
//    fades out over a live map that is already where it is. On first open
//    the real menu panel comes up last.
//
// Years: the opening year of each station from the Swedish Wikipedia list of
// Stockholm metro stations (checked 2026-10-26, the homepage's own table).
// Shared stations carry the year their own line reached them.
//
// Nothing here reads or writes a save, and nothing touches the sim. main.js
// decides when it plays and hands in the theme, the camera and the callbacks.

